/*
:name: spec_parsers_paren_after_typed_decl
:type: comptime
:verifier_pass: 1
:verifier_fail: 0
*/
// docs 02-basics "Newlines and spaces": "If the line starts with an
// alphanumeric ... value or an open parenthesis (`(`), the rest of the line
// belongs to a new statement."
// qa.md chat ruling "Parser consistency: lhd (prpparse) and the tree-sitter
// grammar must be consistent."
//
// The `(` line below is a destructuring statement of its own, also right after
// a declaration whose type could take a `(...)` constraint (`mut x:U8`). The
// comptime harness checks this file twice: as written, and after
// `lhd pyrope fmt` (built on the tree-sitter grammar), so the formatted text
// must keep the two statements apart.
mut r = 0
mut x:U8
(r, x) = (1, 2)
cassert(r == 1 and x == 2)
